name: slice-identity
prereqs: [none — param("slice") is emitted by the parser subscript
  lowering]
invariant: param("slice", NAME, OFF, LEN) folds to the plain read
  param("", NAME) only when NAME is a plain identifier, OFF is a literal
  "0"/"" and LEN is a literal ""/absent — `${v:0:}` and `${v}` expand
  identically in every context. All subscripts/positions/indirections
  (arr[@], @, *, !p, #n), non-literal offsets and non-empty lengths
  (including "0": `${v:0:0}` is empty) are untouched.
scope: offered to all (estree, c, go, java, perl, python, rust, sh,
  fish, zig, zsh, glsl)
updates: none (first offer)